1
00:00:00,060 --> 00:00:01,896
Look! A point.

2
00:00:02,180 --> 00:00:05,306
Woah! It drew a shape.

3
00:00:05,341 --> 00:00:07,908
Let's look at this shape closely.

4
00:00:07,963 --> 00:00:10,614
There are no gaps in its boundary.

5
00:00:10,691 --> 00:00:13,171
Is it open or closed?

6
00:00:13,411 --> 00:00:16,289
Is this shape open or closed?

7
00:00:16,524 --> 00:00:18,121
What about this one?

8
00:00:18,320 --> 00:00:19,588
And this?

9
00:00:19,703 --> 00:00:21,519
How about this one?

10
00:00:21,713 --> 00:00:24,438
These two shapes are open...

11
00:00:24,823 --> 00:00:27,715
...and these two shapes are closed.

12
00:00:27,935 --> 00:00:32,140
Look! The boundaries of the shapes are different too.

13
00:00:32,343 --> 00:00:35,405
Some are straight and some are curved.

14
00:00:35,577 --> 00:00:39,020
Which boundaries are straight and which are curved?

15
00:00:39,681 --> 00:00:45,588
You got it! These boundaries are straight, while these are curved.

16
00:00:45,906 --> 00:00:50,636
Tap the figure that is both closed and made of straight lines.

17
00:00:50,681 --> 00:00:53,260
We call this a polygon.

18
00:00:53,327 --> 00:00:59,407
A closed figure made of only straight line segments is called a polygon.

19
00:00:59,563 --> 00:01:02,370
Which of these figures are polygons?

20
00:01:02,740 --> 00:01:06,396
These line segments are the sides of the polygon.

21
00:01:06,384 --> 00:01:10,839
The point where two sides meet is called a vertex.

22
00:01:10,833 --> 00:01:14,839
When two sides meet, they also form an angle.

23
00:01:15,044 --> 00:01:17,430
Label the parts of the polygon.

24
00:01:17,624 --> 00:01:20,885
How many sides does this polygon have?

25
00:01:21,041 --> 00:01:24,149
This polygon has five sides.

26
00:01:24,173 --> 00:01:26,710
Now let's change how it looks.

27
00:01:26,771 --> 00:01:33,360
Drag any vertex. Stretch it, squash it, or resize it.

28
00:01:33,705 --> 00:01:37,163
Whoa! It looks quite different now.

29
00:01:37,217 --> 00:01:40,340
Its appearance has completely changed.

30
00:01:40,455 --> 00:01:42,927
But not everything has changed.

31
00:01:42,947 --> 00:01:45,177
Let's count the sides again.

32
00:01:45,178 --> 00:01:48,787
Both polygons still have five sides.

33
00:01:48,844 --> 00:01:53,386
So the number of sides gives us a good way to name polygons.

34
00:01:53,411 --> 00:01:57,646
A polygon with three sides is called a triangle.

35
00:01:57,747 --> 00:02:02,273
A polygon with four sides is called a quadrilateral.

36
00:02:02,303 --> 00:02:05,168
Select all the quadrilaterals.

37
00:02:05,290 --> 00:02:09,620
A polygon with five sides is called a pentagon.

38
00:02:09,705 --> 00:02:14,026
A polygon with six sides is called a hexagon.

39
00:02:14,097 --> 00:02:18,539
A polygon with seven sides is called a heptagon.

40
00:02:18,600 --> 00:02:23,171
A polygon with eight sides is called an octagon.

41
00:02:23,334 --> 00:02:27,337
Let's recall the different types of polygons we learnt about.

42
00:02:27,375 --> 00:02:29,861
Which of these is a polygon?

43
00:02:29,914 --> 00:02:34,783
Classify the figures as a polygon or not a polygon.

44
00:02:34,823 --> 00:02:39,825
Find the odd one out. Which figure is NOT a polygon?

45
00:02:40,157 --> 00:02:42,604
Which of these is a pentagon?

46
00:02:42,703 --> 00:02:47,271
Classify each figure as a hexagon or a heptagon.

47
00:02:47,465 --> 00:02:52,314
You did it! Now you know what makes a figure a polygon.

48
00:02:52,362 --> 00:02:56,949
No gaps in its boundary. This shape is closed.

49
00:02:56,969 --> 00:03:00,432
There is a gap in its boundary. It is open.

50
00:03:00,649 --> 00:03:05,802
Not quite. Look for a figure with no gaps and no curves.

51
00:03:05,784 --> 00:03:09,334
Count each side carefully and try again.

52
00:03:09,565 --> 00:03:13,891
Yes! Closed, with only straight sides.

53
00:03:14,041 --> 00:03:18,444
Is it closed? Does it have only straight sides?

54
00:03:18,496 --> 00:03:24,401
A polygon is closed, with only straight sides. Try again.

55
00:03:24,698 --> 00:03:28,629
Great job! You sorted the figures correctly.

56
00:03:28,843 --> 00:03:33,103
Wrong group. Check for gaps or curved sides.

57
00:03:33,092 --> 00:03:38,779
Polygons are closed, with only straight sides. Try again.

58
00:03:38,999 --> 00:03:42,820
You found it! That is not a polygon.

59
00:03:42,910 --> 00:03:46,124
Which figure breaks the rule for a polygon?

60
00:03:46,302 --> 00:03:51,405
Exactly! A pentagon always has five sides.

61
00:03:51,424 --> 00:03:54,512
Count the sides of each figure carefully.

62
00:03:54,479 --> 00:03:58,526
Look for every figure with exactly five sides.

63
00:03:58,684 --> 00:04:05,097
Well done! Hexagons have six sides and heptagons have seven sides.

64
00:04:05,112 --> 00:04:08,273
Count the sides of the ones you placed wrong.

65
00:04:08,278 --> 00:04:12,940
Six sides make a hexagon, seven make a heptagon.

66
00:04:13,120 --> 00:04:15,584
Yes! It is closed.

67
00:04:15,800 --> 00:04:18,002
Yes! It is open.

68
00:04:18,185 --> 00:04:23,954
Look! This boundary isn't curved. It is made of straight lines.

69
00:04:24,154 --> 00:04:30,191
Look closely. This boundary bends smoothly. It is curved.

70
00:04:30,508 --> 00:04:34,622
Yes! It is closed and made of straight lines.

71
00:04:34,801 --> 00:04:37,922
That is right! These are the ones.

72
00:04:37,931 --> 00:04:42,353
A polygon is closed, with only straight sides.

73
00:04:42,521 --> 00:04:48,259
Perfect! Side, vertex and angle — all labelled.

74
00:04:48,462 --> 00:04:53,866
Not that one. A side is straight, a vertex is a corner.

75
00:04:54,131 --> 00:04:56,477
Not quite. Try again.

